Task: Layer boundary check and core coverage (Phase 2)

Red phase: tests first, failed on the missing module. Green phase: eight new
tests pass, fifty-three in total.

The checker was also proved end to end rather than only through its unit tests:
run against the real core it reports clean and exits zero; with a deliberate
violation appended to one module it names the file and line and exits non-zero;
with the violation removed it is clean again.

Why it needed care:
A naive search would report the word 'application' in every module's own
comments, and prose in a message string, and a parameter that happens to share
a name. Each of those is a separate test, because any one of them would produce
noise that makes the gate useless.

Coverage:
Measured over the core layer only, which is where the target applies - the
application-facing layers cannot be exercised outside the application and
counting them would turn a meaningful number into a meaningless one. Every core
module is fully covered, against a target of eighty percent.

The test runner now also discovers tests for the tooling, not just the core.
